+# Wire format
+
+Muninn's recorded decision (`docs/format.md`, `design/ENGINE.md` §9) is that SQLite is the operational store and is never the wire format: every record is projected as Markdown with a YAML frontmatter (`kind, subject, relation, object, origin, trust, anchor_path, anchor_hash, created_at, invalid, invalid_reason, invalidated_by`, plus a literal body) under `.muninn/records/<kind>/<id>.md`, and full interchange goes through JSONL — `muninn export` writes one JSON object per record to `.muninn/export-<timestamp>.jsonl`, and `muninn import` accepts that JSONL or a directory of frontmatter Markdown. No proprietary fields live in the container itself; the differentiators (cues, the subject/relation/object triple, provenance) are carried in fields so that if the W3C AI Agent Memory Interoperability Community Group or a similar effort (e.g. PAM) settles on a standard, the projection can change without altering the internal schema.
